    "baseRefOid": "aac6760e032050dd47f5dbd32f852bf1ede9312b",
    "body": "As per [RFC 8441](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8441#section-4):\r\n\r\n> On requests that contain the :protocol pseudo-header field, the\r\n      :scheme and :path pseudo-header fields of the target URI (see\r\n      [Section 5](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8441#section-5)) MUST also be included.\r\n\r\nI was trying to implement WebSocket handshake based on HTTP/2 Extended CONNECT. The current implementation crafted a request which was considered invalid by the server (HAProxy 2.8):\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/hyperium/hyper/assets/5270106/6157bc77-8bb6-47aa-936d-275dd4af761c)\r\n\r\nCompared to the [example](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8441#section-5.1) illustrated in RFC 8441, the pseudo headers `:scheme` and `:path` were missing.\r\n\r\nAfter the fix, the client could successfully establish a WebSocket tunnel to the server.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/hyperium/hyper/assets/5270106/80ebc989-7e2b-4720-870e-9fcdec22faea)\r\n",
